{"schemaVersion":1,"durationMinutes":30,"audioUrl":"","parts":[{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-p1","title":"Part 1","part_number":1,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3172229-cambridge-ielts-05-academic-listening-test-2-1.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-g1-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 1-10","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>LIBRARY INFORMATION</strong></p><table><tbody><tr><td>Example<p></p><p>Minimum joining age:</p></td><td>Answer<p></p><p>18 years</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>For registration, must take</p><ul><li>two <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">1</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q1\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and</li><li>two forms of I.D. e.g. driving licence, <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">2</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q2\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p>Cost to join per year (without current student card): £ <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">3</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q3\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>Number of items allowed: (members of public) <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">4</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q4\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>Loan times: four weeks</p><p>Fines start at £ <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">5</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q5\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>Computers can be booked up to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">6</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q6\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> hours in advance</p><p>Library holds most national papers, all <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">7</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q7\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, and magazines</p><p>Need <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">8</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q8\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> to use photocopier</p><p><b>Creative Writing class</b></p><ul><li>tutor is John <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">9</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q9\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li><li>held on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">10</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q10\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> evenings</li></ul></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-05-academic-listening-test-2-1.mp3"],"order_index":1},{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-p2","title":"Part 2","part_number":2,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3172230-cambridge-ielts-05-academic-listening-test-2-2.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-g2-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 11-15","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Choose the correct letter, A, B or C.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">11</strong> In 1993 Dan Pearman went to Ecuador</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q11\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>as a tourist guide.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q11\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>as part of his studies.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q11\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>as a voluntary worker.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">12</strong> Dan's neighbour was successful in business because he</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q12\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>employed carpenters from the area.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q12\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>was the most skilled craftsman in the town.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q12\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>found it easy to reach customers.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">13</strong> Dan says the charity relies on</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q13\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>getting enough bicycles to send regularly.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q13\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>finding new areas which need the bicycles.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q13\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>charging for the bicycles it sends abroad.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">14</strong> What does Dan say about the town of Rivas?</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q14\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>It has received the greatest number of bikes.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q14\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>It has almost as many bikes as Amsterdam.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q14\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>Its economy has been totally transformed.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">15</strong> What problem did the charity face in August 2000?</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q15\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>It couldn't meet its overheads.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q15\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>It had to delay sending the bikes.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q15\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>It was criticised in the British media.</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5},{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-g2-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 16-17","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Answer the questions below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN ONE WORD OR A NUMBER for each answer.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">16</strong><span>How much money in pounds did the charity receive when it won an award?</span></span><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q16\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">17</strong><span>What is the charity currently hoping to buy?</span></span><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q17\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":2},{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-g2-2","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 18-20","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Choose THREE letters A-G.</p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">18</strong><strong class=\"source-question-number\">19</strong><strong class=\"source-question-number\">20</strong> Which THREE things can the general public do to help the charity Pedal Power?</span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q18\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>organise a bicycle collection</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q18\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>repair the donated bikes</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q18\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>donate their unwanted tools</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">D</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q18\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"D\"></span><span>do voluntary work in its office</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">E</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q18\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"E\"></span><span>hold an event to raise money</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">F</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q18\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"F\"></span><span>identify areas that need bikes</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">G</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q18\" data-luma-kind=\"checkbox\" data-luma-option=\"G\"></span><span>write to the government</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":1}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-05-academic-listening-test-2-2.mp3"],"order_index":2},{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-p3","title":"Part 3","part_number":3,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3172231-cambridge-ielts-05-academic-listening-test-2-3.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-g3-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 21-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>Complete the table below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>'Student Life' video project</strong></p><table><tbody><tr><th></th><th>Cristina</th><th>Ibrahim</th></tr><tr><td>Enjoyed:</td><td><ul><li>using the camera</li><li>going to a British <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">21</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul></td><td>contact with students doing other courses (has asked some to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">22</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> with him)</td></tr><tr><td>Most useful language practice:</td><td><ul><li>listening to instructions</li><li>learning <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">23</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> vocabulary</li></ul></td><td>listening to British students' language because of:<p></p><p>- normal speed</p><p>- large amount of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p></td></tr><tr><td>General usefulness:</td><td><ul><li>operating video camera</li><li>working with other people:<p></p><p>- learning about <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></p><p>- compromising</p><p>- <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> people who have different views</p></li></ul></td><td>the importance of <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></td></tr><tr><td>Things to do differently in future:</td><td><ul><li>decide when to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> each stage at the beginning</li><li>make more effort to <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> with the camera</li></ul></td><td>don't make the film too <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-05-academic-listening-test-2-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/3172232-cambridge-ielts-05-academic-listening-test-2-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"table_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write NO MORE THAN THREE WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER for each answer.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong>ANTARCTICA</strong></p><p><b>GEOGRAPHY</b></p><ul><li>world's highest, coldest and windiest continent</li><li>more than <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> times as big as the UK</li><li>most of the area is classified as <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span></li></ul><p><b>RESEARCH STATIONS</b></p><ul><li>international teams work together</li><li><span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> is integrated with technical support</li><li>stations contain accommodation, work areas, a kitchen, a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> and a gym</li><li>supplies were brought to Zero One station by sledge from a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> at the edge of the ice 15 km away</li><li>problem of snow build-ups solved by building stations on <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> with adjustable legs</li></ul><p><b>FOOD AND DIET</b></p><ul><li>average daily requirement for an adult in Antarctica is approximately <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> kilocalories</li><li>rations for field work prepared by process of freeze-drying</li></ul><p><b>RESEARCH</b></p><p>The most important research focuses on climate change, including</p><ul><li>measuring changes in the ice-cap (because of effects on sea levels and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>)</li><li>monitoring the hole in the ozone layer</li><li>analysing air from bubbles in ice to measure <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> caused by human activity</li></ul><p><b>WORK OPPORTUNITIES</b></p><p>Many openings for <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c5-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span> people including</p><ul><li>research assistants</li><li>administrative and technical positions</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/cambridge-ielts-05-academic-listening-test-2-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c5-t2-l-q1","part_id":"en-c5-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c5-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"passport photos/photos/passport photographs/photographs","correct_answer_variants":["passport photos","photos","passport p